1
00:00:03,054 --> 00:00:06,799
This morning, Noah drew around the puddle with chalk.

2
00:00:06,849 --> 00:00:07,873
This afternoon…

3
00:00:07,923 --> 00:00:09,498
the puddle has shrunk!

4
00:00:10,288 --> 00:00:11,326
Nobody drank it.

5
00:00:11,376 --> 00:00:12,347
It didn't rain.

6
00:00:12,397 --> 00:00:13,962
Where did the water go?

7
00:00:14,789 --> 00:00:15,889
Mila has an idea:

8
00:00:15,939 --> 00:00:18,123
the water went into the sidewalk!

9
00:00:18,173 --> 00:00:20,424
But the concrete is hard, and dry.

10
00:00:20,474 --> 00:00:21,421
That's not it.

11
00:00:22,192 --> 00:00:23,706
Discovery mission!

12
00:00:27,222 --> 00:00:27,794
Mini mode!

13
00:00:27,844 --> 00:00:31,404
Water is made of billions of tiny drops, called molecules,

14
00:00:31,454 --> 00:00:33,694
that move and hold on to each other.

15
00:00:34,519 --> 00:00:35,747
The Sun warms them up.

16
00:00:35,797 --> 00:00:37,374
They move faster and faster.

17
00:00:37,424 --> 00:00:38,827
And the ones on top break

18
00:00:38,877 --> 00:00:40,620
free and fly off into the air!

19
00:00:41,492 --> 00:00:43,554
We can't see them: in the air,

20
00:00:43,604 --> 00:00:44,892
water is invisible.

21
00:00:44,942 --> 00:00:47,054
But it's there, all around us.

22
00:00:47,824 --> 00:00:49,394
Way up high, it's cold.

23
00:00:49,444 --> 00:00:52,987
The molecules gather into droplets: that's a cloud.

24
00:00:53,037 --> 00:00:55,572
And one day, they fall back as rain.

25
00:00:56,358 --> 00:00:58,444
That's where the puddle's water goes:

26
00:00:58,494 --> 00:01:00,399
into the sky, to come back later.

27
00:01:01,232 --> 00:01:04,074
Water doesn't disappear: it flies off into the air,

28
00:01:04,124 --> 00:01:06,278
invisible, and will come back as rain.

29
00:01:07,099 --> 00:01:09,799
With an adult: two glasses of water,

30
00:01:09,849 --> 00:01:10,869
a marker line.

31
00:01:10,919 --> 00:01:13,390
One in the sun, one in the shade.

32
00:01:13,440 --> 00:01:14,968
Compare in two days!

33
00:01:15,754 --> 00:01:17,887
And why does ice float on water?

34
00:01:17,937 --> 00:01:19,302
The answer tomorrow.
